Fix the following CTL2 ROLLUP transform so that it compiles and does what the specification says. List every problem you fix with the reason, then give the complete corrected code.

Specification:
1. Input ReceiptLine has warehouse_id (string, non-null), receipt_id (long), received_units (integer, nullable), and unit_cost (decimal, non-null). Records are grouped by warehouse_id; each group has at least one line. Accumulator ReceiptAcc has warehouse_id (string), line_count (integer), counted_lines (integer), and inventory_value (decimal).
2. Capture warehouse_id from the first line of each group; line_count counts all lines in that group.
3. A null received_units contributes zero units and zero inventory value, and does not increment counted_lines. A non-null received_units increments counted_lines and contributes received_units * unit_cost to inventory_value.
4. Output WarehouseSummary has warehouse_id (string), line_count (integer), counted_lines (integer), inventory_value (decimal), and average_value (decimal). average_value is inventory_value / counted_lines, or 0D when counted_lines is zero.
5. Produce no per-line output and exactly one summary row when each group finishes.

Current transform:
```ctl
//#CTL2:COMPILE
function void initGroup(ReceiptAcc acc) {
    acc.warehouse_id = null;
    acc.line_count = "0";
    acc.counted_lines = 0;
    acc.inventory_value = 0D;
}
function boolean updateGroup(ReceiptAcc acc) {
    acc.line_count = acc.line_count + 1;
    acc.counted_lines = acc.counted_lines + 1;
    acc.inventory_value = acc.inventory_value + $in.0.received_units * $in.0.unit_cost;
    return false;
}
function boolean finishGroup(ReceiptAcc acc) { return true; }
function integer updateTransform(integer counter, ReceiptAcc acc) { return SKIP; }
function integer transform(integer counter, ReceiptAcc acc) {
    $out.0.warehouse_id = acc.warehouse_id;
    $out.0.line_count = acc.line_count;
    $out.0.counted_lines = acc.counted_lines;
    $out.0.inventory_value = acc.inventory_value;
    $out.0.average_value = acc.counted_lines == 0 ? 0D : acc.inventory_value / acc.line_count;
    return ALL;
}
```

Fix the following CTL2 Rollup transform so that it compiles and does what the specification says. List every problem you fix with the reason, then give the complete corrected code.

Specification:
1. Input port 0 is turbine service work, grouped by turbine_id: turbine_id string non-null, work_order string non-null, state string non-null, service_cost decimal nullable. state is OPEN or VOID. Groups are contiguous and contain at least one row.
2. The Rollup accumulator metadata is a Record named ServiceAcc with turbine_id string, valid_count integer, total_cost decimal, and average_cost decimal. Output port 0 has turbine_id string, valid_count integer, total_cost decimal, and average_cost decimal.
3. Ignore VOID work orders entirely. For each OPEN work order increment valid_count; a null service_cost contributes zero to total_cost.
4. After the group, set average_cost to total_cost divided by valid_count, or zero when valid_count is zero. Round the average half-up to two decimal places.
5. Emit exactly one summary row for each group, including zero-valid-order groups. Copy turbine_id and all three accumulator measures into the output.
6. Produce no per-work-order detail rows.

Candidate transform:
```ctl
//#CTL2
function void initGroup(ServiceAcc acc) {
    acc.turbine_id = "";
    acc.valid_count = 0;
    acc.total_cost = 0.0D;
    acc.average_cost = 0.0D;
}
function boolean updateGroup(ServiceAcc acc) {
    acc.turbine_id = $in.0.turbine_id;
    acc.valid_count = acc.valid_count + 1;
    acc.total_cost = acc.total_cost + $in.0.service_cost;
    return false;
}
function boolean finishGroup(ServiceAcc acc) {
    acc.average_cost = round(acc.total_cost / (acc.valid_count + 1), 2);
    return false;
}
function integer updateTransform(integer counter, ServiceAcc acc) {
    return SKIP;
}
function integer transform(integer counter, ServiceAcc acc) {
    $out.0.turbine_id = acc.turbine_id;
    $out.0.valid_count = acc.valid_count;
    $out.0.total_cost = acc.total_cost;
    $out.0.average_cost = acc.average_cost;
    return ALL;
}
```

Fix the following CTL2 PARTITION transform so that it compiles and does what the specification says. List every problem you fix with the reason, then give the complete corrected code.

Specification:
1. Input IncidentIn has incident_id (long), severity (integer, nullable), region (string, nullable), and confidential (boolean, non-null). The Partition has output ports 0 through 4 and routes each input to exactly one zero-based port.
2. Confidential incidents always route to port 0, regardless of severity or region.
3. Among non-confidential incidents, severity at least 8 routes to port 1. If severity is null, route to port 2, even when region is "EU".
4. Remaining incidents with region exactly "EU" route to port 3; all other remaining incidents, including null region, route to port 4.
5. The CTL must only choose a port; it must not write output fields.

Current transform:
```ctl
//#CTL2
function integer getOutputPort() {
    if ($in.0.severity > 8) return 1;
    if ($in.0.confidential) return 0;
    if ($in.0.region == "EU") return 3;
    if (isnull($in.0.severity)) return 2;
    return 4;
}
```

Fix the following CTL2 Partition transform so that it compiles and does what the specification says. List every problem you fix with the reason, then give the complete corrected code.

Specification:
1. Input port 0 is a wildfire smoke sensor reading: sensor_id string, pm25 integer nullable, muted boolean non-null.
2. There are exactly three output ports, numbered 0 for critical, 1 for caution, and 2 for routine.
3. Muted readings always route to routine port 2, regardless of pm25.
4. Unmuted readings with null pm25 also route to routine port 2.
5. For unmuted non-null pm25, values at least 80 route to critical port 0, values from 40 through 79 route to caution port 1, and values below 40 route to routine port 2.
6. Routing does not alter the record.

Candidate transform:
```ctl
//#CTL2
function integer getOutputPort() {
    if ($in.0.muted) return 0;
    if ($in.0.pm25 > 80) return 0;
    if ($in.0.pm25 >= 40) return 1;
    return 2;
}
```

Fix the following CTL2 ROLLUP transform so that it compiles and does what the specification says. List every problem you fix with the reason, then give the complete corrected code.

Input port 0 contains zone_id: long (non-null), fine: integer (nullable), paid: boolean (non-null), and voided: boolean (non-null). Input is sorted and grouped by zone_id. The Rollup accumulator metadata is named ZoneAcc and declares zone_id: long, citation_count: integer, outstanding_total: integer, high_unpaid_count: integer. Output port 0 has the same four fields, all non-null.

Specification:
1. Emit exactly one summary row per zone, including a zone whose citations are all voided.
2. citation_count counts every non-voided citation, whether paid or unpaid.
3. outstanding_total sums fine only for non-voided unpaid citations, treating a null fine as zero.
4. high_unpaid_count counts non-voided unpaid citations whose non-null fine is strictly greater than 200.
5. Use zone_id from the grouped input; initialize each accumulator field for every group.

Current transform:
```ctl
//#CTL2
function void initGroup(ZoneAcc acc) {
    acc.zone_id = 0L;
    acc.citation_count = 0;
    acc.outstanding_total = 0;
    acc.high_unpaid_count = 0;
}
function boolean updateGroup(ZoneAcc acc) {
    acc.zone_id = $in.0.zone_id;
    if ($in.0.voided && $in.0.paid) return false;
    acc.citation_count++;
    acc.outstanding_total += $in.0.fine;
    if (!$in.0.paid && !isnull($in.0.fine) && $in.0.fine >= 200) acc.high_unpaid_count++;
    return false;
}
function boolean finishGroup(ZoneAcc acc) { return true; }
function integer updateTransform(integer counter, ZoneAcc acc) { return SKIP; }
function integer transform(integer counter, ZoneAcc acc) {
    $out.0.zone_id = acc.zone_id;
    $out.0.citation_count = acc.citation_count;
    $out.0.outstanding_total = acc.outstanding_total;
    $out.0.high_unpaid_count = acc.high_unpaid_count;
    return ALL;
}
```

Fix the following CTL2 Hash Join transform so that it compiles and does what the specification says. List every problem you fix with the reason, then give the complete corrected code.

Specification:
1. This is a left Hash Join of fisheries catch rows on master port 0 with optional quota rows on slave port 1, keyed by species_code. Master fields: landing_id string non-null, species_code string non-null, zone string non-null, caught_kg decimal non-null. Slave fields: species_code string nullable when unmatched, quota_kg decimal nullable when unmatched.
2. Output port 0 has landing_id string, species_code string, zone string, quota_kg decimal, over_quota boolean, and quota_matched boolean.
3. Preserve landing_id, species_code, and zone exactly from the master row. Every master row emits one output row, including unmatched rows.
4. quota_kg is the slave quota when present, otherwise zero. quota_matched is true exactly when a slave species_code exists.
5. over_quota is true only when caught_kg is strictly greater than effective quota_kg. A catch equal to quota is not over quota.

Candidate transform:
```ctl
//#CTL2:COMPILE
function integer transform() {
    $out.0.landing_id = $in.0.landing_id;
    $out.0.species_code = $in.1.species_code;
    $out.0.zone = $in.0.zone;
    $out.0.quota_kg = $in.1.quota_kg;
    $out.0.over_quota = $in.0.caught_kg >= nvl($in.1.quota_kg, 0.0D);
    return ALL;
}
```

Fix the following CTL2 HASH_JOIN transform so that it compiles and does what the specification says. List every problem you fix with the reason, then give the complete corrected code.

Specification:
1. This is a left outer Hash Join. Master InvoiceIn on port 0 has invoice_id (long), vendor_id (string, non-null), and net_total (decimal, non-null). Optional slave VendorRate on port 1 has vendor_id (string, nullable when absent) and rebate_pct (decimal, nullable). Output RebateOut has invoice_id (long), vendor_id (string), effective_rate (decimal), rebate_amount (decimal), and status (string).
2. Copy invoice_id and vendor_id from the master on every output row, including unmatched invoices.
3. A missing slave vendor_id means no policy: effective_rate and rebate_amount are 0D, status is "NO_POLICY".
4. With a matched policy, a null rebate_pct means 0D. Only invoices with net_total strictly greater than 1000D qualify; for them effective_rate is the policy percentage and rebate_amount is net_total times that rate divided by 100D, status "ELIGIBLE".
5. Matched invoices at or below 1000D have effective_rate and rebate_amount 0D and status "BELOW_MIN". Emit exactly one row for each master invoice.

Current transform:
```ctl
//#CTL2:COMPILE
function integer transform() {
    $out.0.invoice_id = $in.0.invoice_id;
    $out.0.vendor_id = $in.1.vendor_id;
    if (isnull($in.1.vendor_id)) {
        $out.0.effective_rate = 0D;
        $out.0.rebate_amount = 0D;
        $out.0.status = "NO_POLICY";
    } else if ($in.0.net_total >= 1000D) {
        $out.0.effective_rate = $in.1.rebate_pct;
        $out.0.rebate_amount = $in.0.net_total * $in.1.rebate_pct / 100D;
        $out.0.status = "ELIGIBLE";
    } else {
        $out.0.effective_rate = $in.1.rebate_pct;
        $out.0.rebate_amount = 0D;
        $out.0.status = "BELOW_MIN";
    }
    return ALL;
}
```

Fix the following CTL2 Reformat transform so that it compiles and does what the specification says. List every problem you fix with the reason, then give the complete corrected code.

Specification:
1. Input port 0 is a greenhouse water invoice: invoice_id string, account_name string, reading_date date, litres integer, unit_rate decimal, status string. All except account_name are non-null; account_name may be null. Status is either ACTIVE or CANCELLED.
2. Output port 0 has invoice_id string, account_name string, period string, water_charge decimal, and billed_litres integer.
3. CANCELLED invoices produce no output. ACTIVE invoices produce exactly one output row.
4. Copy invoice_id and litres to invoice_id and billed_litres; set account_name to uppercase trimmed input, or UNKNOWN when input is null.
5. Format period from reading_date as four-digit year, hyphen, two-digit month (yyyy-MM).
6. Calculate water_charge as litres times unit_rate, rounded half-up to two decimal places.

Candidate transform:
```ctl
//#CTL2:COMPILE
function integer transform() {
    $out.0.invoice_id = $in.0.invoice_id;
    $out.0.billed_litres = $in.0.litres;
    $out.0.account_name = upperCase(trim($in.0.account_name));
    $out.0.period = date2str($in.0.reading_date, "yyyy-mm");
    $out.0.water_charge = round($in.0.litres * $in.0.unit_rate, 1);
    return ALL;
}
```

Fix the following CTL2 ROLLUP transform so that it compiles and does what the specification says. List every problem you fix with the reason, then give the complete corrected code.

Specification:
1. Input VisitIn has clinic_id (string, non-null), visit_id (long), wait_minutes (integer, nullable), and urgent (boolean, non-null). Input is grouped by clinic_id, with at least one visit per group. Accumulator VisitAcc has clinic_id (string), visit_count (integer), long_wait_count (integer), and urgent_count (integer).
2. Capture clinic_id from the first visit and count every visit in visit_count.
3. Count a long wait only when wait_minutes is non-null and strictly greater than 30. Count every urgent visit regardless of its wait_minutes.
4. Output VisitSummary has clinic_id, visit_count, long_wait_count, and urgent_count, with matching types.
5. Emit no per-visit output and one summary row per group.

Current transform:
```ctl
//#CTL2
function void initGroup(VisitAcc acc) {
    acc.clinic_id = null;
    acc.visit_count = 0;
    acc.long_wait_count = 0;
    acc.urgent_count = 0;
}
function boolean updateGroup(VisitAcc acc) {
    if (acc.visit_count == 0) acc.clinic_id = $in.0.clinic_id;
    acc.visit_count = acc.visit_count + 1;
    if (!isnull($in.0.wait_minutes) && $in.0.wait_minutes >= 30) acc.long_wait_count = acc.long_wait_count + 1;
    if ($in.0.urgent && !isnull($in.0.wait_minutes)) acc.urgent_count = acc.urgent_count + 1;
    return false;
}
function boolean finishGroup(VisitAcc acc) { return true; }
function integer updateTransform(integer counter, VisitAcc acc) { return SKIP; }
function integer transform(integer counter, VisitAcc acc) {
    if (counter > 0) return SKIP;
    $out.0.clinic_id = acc.clinic_id;
    $out.0.visit_count = acc.visit_count;
    $out.0.long_wait_count = acc.long_wait_count;
    $out.0.urgent_count = acc.long_wait_count;
    return ALL;
}
```

Fix the following CTL2 REFORMAT transform so that it compiles and does what the specification says. List every problem you fix with the reason, then give the complete corrected code.

Input port 0 has vessel_id: long, engine_hours: integer, hull_grade: string (nullable), inspection_due: date (nullable); all fields except the noted ones are non-null. Output port 0 has vessel_id: long, service_class: string, corrosion_flag: boolean, next_check: date (nullable), and maintenance_points: integer.

Specification:
1. Copy vessel_id unchanged.
2. service_class is HIGH only when engine_hours is strictly greater than 500; otherwise ROUTINE.
3. corrosion_flag is true when hull_grade, after trimming and uppercasing, equals C. A null grade is not C.
4. next_check is 30 calendar days after a non-null inspection_due; a null due date remains null.
5. maintenance_points is max(engine_hours - 100, 0).

Current transform:
```ctl
//#CTL2:COMPILE
function integer transform() {
    $out.0.vessel_id = $in.0.vessel_id;
    $out.0.service_class = $in.0.engine_hours >= 500 ? "HIGH" : "ROUTINE";
    $out.0.corrosion_flag = $in.0.hull_grade == "C";
    $out.0.next_check = isnull($in.0.inspection_due) ? null : dateAdd($in.0.inspection_due, 7L, day);
    $out.0.maintenance_points = $in.0.engine_hours > 100 ? $in.0.engine_hours / 100 : 0;
    return ALL;
}
```

Fix the following CTL2 EXT_HASH_JOIN transform so that it compiles and does what the specification says. List every problem you fix with the reason, then give the complete corrected code.

This is a left outer ExtHashJoin. Port 0 master metadata has permit_id: long (non-null), district_code: string (non-null), base_fee: integer (non-null, nonnegative), bike_type: string (non-null), and violation_count: integer (non-null, nonnegative). Port 1 slave metadata has district_code: string (non-null in a matched row; null when unmatched), fee_addon: integer (nullable), and waive_electric: boolean (nullable). Output port 0 has permit_id: long, district_code: string, due_fee: integer, and policy_status: string. The configured join key is district_code.

Specification:
1. Emit one output for every master permit, including unmatched district policies; copy permit_id and the master district_code.
2. Base due_fee is base_fee plus fee_addon; use zero addon when the slave row or fee_addon is absent.
3. If bike_type is ELECTRIC and the matched policy has waive_electric true, waive the base-plus-addon portion. Otherwise retain it.
4. Add 10 for each violation regardless of any electric waiver.
5. policy_status is UNMAPPED only for an unmatched slave row; otherwise ACTIVE. Presence is determined by the concrete slave district_code field.

Current transform:
```ctl
//#CTL2:COMPILE
function integer transform() {
    $out.0.permit_id = $in.0.permit_id;
    $out.0.district_code = $in.1.district_code;
    integer due = $in.0.base_fee - nvl($in.1.fee_addon, 0);
    if ($in.1.waive_electric == true) due = 0;
    due = due + 10 * ($in.0.violation_count - 1);
    $out.0.due_fee = due;
    $out.0.policy_status = isnull($in.1.district_code) ? "ACTIVE" : "UNMAPPED";
    return ALL;
}
```

Fix the following CTL2 REFORMAT transform so that it compiles and does what the specification says. List every problem you fix with the reason, then give the complete corrected code.

Specification:
1. Input TicketIn has ticket_id (long), base_price (decimal, non-null), discount_pct (decimal, nullable), visitor_age (integer, non-null), and visit_date (date, nullable). Output TicketOut has ticket_id (long), net_price (decimal), age_band (string), and visit_month (string).
2. Copy ticket_id unchanged and calculate net_price as base_price times (100 minus discount_pct) divided by 100, rounded half-up to two decimal places. A null discount_pct means zero discount.
3. A visitor aged 12 or younger has age_band "CHILD"; every older visitor has "ADULT".
4. For a non-null visit_date, visit_month is its calendar month as two digits. For a null visit_date, visit_month is the empty string.
5. Emit exactly one output row for every input ticket.

Current transform:
```ctl
//#CTL2:COMPILE
function integer transform() {
    $out.0.ticket_id = $in.0.ticket_id;
    $out.0.net_price = round($in.0.base_price * (100D - $in.0.discount_pct) / 100D, 0);
    $out.0.age_band = $in.0.visitor_age < 12 ? "CHILD" : "ADULT";
    $out.0.visit_month = isnull($in.0.visit_date) ? "" : date2str($in.0.visit_date, "mm");
    return ALL;
}
```

Fix the following CTL2 Normalizer transform so that it compiles and does what the specification says. List every problem you fix with the reason, then give the complete corrected code.

Specification:
1. Input port 0 is one school assessment: student_id string non-null, mathematics integer nullable, reading integer nullable, science integer nullable.
2. Output port 0 has student_id string, subject string, score integer, ordinal integer, and passed boolean.
3. Produce one row for each non-null score only, in mathematics, reading, science order. If all scores are null, produce zero rows.
4. subject is exactly MATHEMATICS, READING, or SCIENCE for its source score; score is that source value.
5. ordinal is one-based among emitted rows, without gaps caused by absent scores.
6. passed is true for a score of at least 50, and false below 50. Every output row copies student_id.

Candidate transform:
```ctl
//#CTL2
function integer count() {
    return 3;
}
function integer transform(integer idx) {
    if (idx == 0) {
        $out.0.subject = "MATHEMATICS";
        $out.0.score = $in.0.mathematics;
    } else if (idx == 1) {
        $out.0.subject = "WRITING";
        $out.0.score = $in.0.reading;
    } else {
        $out.0.subject = "SCIENCE";
        $out.0.score = $in.0.science;
    }
    $out.0.ordinal = idx;
    $out.0.passed = $out.0.score > 50;
    return OK;
}
```

Fix the following CTL2 DataGenerator transform so that it compiles and does what the specification says. List every problem you fix with the reason, then give the complete corrected code.

Specification:
1. This DataGenerator is configured to call generate() exactly four times. It has no input port. Output port 0 has shift_no long, site_code string, shift_date date, paid_hours decimal, and roster_key string.
2. shift_no starts at 7001 on the first call and increments by one on each later call.
3. site_code alternates A, B, A, B beginning with A on the first call.
4. shift_date starts on 2026-01-05 and advances one calendar day per generated row.
5. paid_hours is 6.0 on every third row and 8.0 on all other rows.
6. roster_key is the literal `SHIFT-` followed by the current shift_no. Each call emits one complete row.

Candidate transform:
```ctl
//#CTL2:COMPILE
long nextShift = 7001L;
integer rowNumber = 0;
date nextDate = 2026-01-05;
function integer generate() {
    nextShift = nextShift + 1L;
    rowNumber = rowNumber + 1;
    $out.0.shift_no = nextShift;
    $out.0.site_code = rowNumber % 2 == 0 ? "A" : "B";
    $out.0.shift_date = nextDate;
    nextDate = dateAdd(nextDate, 2L, day);
    $out.0.paid_hours = rowNumber % 3 == 0 ? 6.0D : 7.5D;
    $out.0.roster_key = $out.0.site_code + "-" + $out.0.shift_no;
    return OK;
}
```

Fix the following CTL2 DENORMALIZER transform so that it compiles and does what the specification says. List every problem you fix with the reason, then give the complete corrected code.

Input port 0 has venue_id: long (non-null), show_id: string (non-null), start_time: date (nullable), cancelled: boolean (non-null), and seats: integer (non-null), sorted and grouped by venue_id. Every group has at least one input row. Output port 0 has venue_id: long, scheduled_count: integer, first_show: date (nullable), seat_total: integer, and show_ids: string.

Specification:
1. Emit exactly one row for every venue, even when no show qualifies.
2. A show qualifies only when cancelled is false and start_time is non-null.
3. scheduled_count counts qualifying shows, and seat_total sums seats only for qualifying shows.
4. first_show is the earliest start_time among qualifying shows, or null if there are none.
5. show_ids concatenates qualifying show_id values in input order, separated by commas; use an empty string if none qualify.
6. Reset all per-venue state before the next group.

Current transform:
```ctl
//#CTL2:COMPILE
long venueId;
integer scheduledCount = 0;
integer seatTotal = 0;
date firstShow = null;
string showIds = "";
function integer append() {
    venueId = $in.0.venue_id;
    seatTotal += $in.0.seats;
    if ($in.0.cancelled || !isnull($in.0.start_time)) {
        if (scheduledCount == 0) showIds = $in.0.show_id;
        else showIds = showIds + "," + $in.0.show_id;
        scheduledCount++;
        if (!isnull($in.0.start_time) && (isnull(firstShow) || $in.0.start_time < earliestShow)) firstShow = $in.0.start_time;
    }
    return OK;
}
function integer transform() {
    $out.0.venue_id = venueId;
    $out.0.scheduled_count = scheduledCount;
    $out.0.first_show = firstShow;
    $out.0.seat_total = seatTotal;
    $out.0.show_ids = showIds;
    return OK;
}
function void clean() {
    venueId = 0L;
    scheduledCount = 0;
    seatTotal = 0;
    firstShow = null;
}
```

Fix the following CTL2 NORMALIZER transform so that it compiles and does what the specification says. List every problem you fix with the reason, then give the complete corrected code.

Specification:
1. Input ContactIn has customer_id (long), active (boolean, non-null), primary_email (string, nullable), secondary_email (string, nullable), and mobile (string, nullable). Output ContactOut has customer_id (long), method (string), address (string), and ordinal (integer).
2. Inactive customers produce zero rows. Active customers produce one row for each non-null, non-empty contact slot; whitespace-only values are allowed and become empty after trimming.
3. The output order is primary_email, then secondary_email, then mobile. Use method "EMAIL" for either email slot and "PHONE" for mobile.
4. Trim leading and trailing whitespace from each emitted address, and copy customer_id unchanged.
5. ordinal is one-based among the rows actually emitted for that input, with no gaps. An active customer with no qualifying slots produces zero rows.

Current transform:
```ctl
//#CTL2
string[] addresses = [];
string[] methods = [];
function integer count() {
    addresses = [];
    methods = [];
    if (!isnull($in.0.secondary_email)) {
        addresses = append(addresses, $in.0.secondary_email);
        methods = append(methods, "EMAIL");
    }
    if (!isnull($in.0.primary_email)) {
        addresses = append(addresses, $in.0.primary_email);
        methods = append(methods, "EMAIL");
    }
    if (!isnull($in.0.mobile)) {
        addresses = append(addresses, $in.0.mobile);
        methods = append(methods, "PHONE");
    }
    return length(addresses);
}
function integer transform(integer idx) {
    $out.0.customer_id = $in.0.customer_id;
    $out.0.method = methods[idx];
    $out.0.address = addresses[idx];
    $out.0.ordinal = idx;
    return OK;
