Business logic:
- A missing civil-servant record routes to HOLD with zero credited_duty_hours and compensatory_credit, using STAFF_RECORD_MISSING as the justification_code. A missing municipal-office record also routes to HOLD with zero values and OFFICE_RECORD_MISSING. Use civil-servant precedence.
- For matched records, route to UNASSIGNABLE with zero values and OUTSIDE_APPOINTMENT when appointment_state is not APPOINTED, or when duty_day is before service_from, or when duty_day is after a non-null service_until.
- Also route to UNASSIGNABLE with zero values and COUNTER_ACCESS_RESTRICTED when duty_class starts with PUBLIC_COUNTER and access_level is CLOSED.
- Otherwise, credited_duty_hours is planned_duty_hours multiplied by 1.25 for a crisis_desk office; for every other office it is planned_duty_hours. Round credited_duty_hours to two decimals.
- compensatory_credit is zero when flex_time_balance is null; otherwise it is the lower of flex_time_balance and credited_duty_hours.
- Route to MUNICIPAL_COORDINATION when duty_class starts with CROSS_MUNICIPAL, or when remote_authorised is true and crisis_desk is false. Otherwise route to SCHEDULED. Use CROSS_MUNICIPAL_DUTY as the justification_code for MUNICIPAL_COORDINATION and null for SCHEDULED.

